the graders' own totals, for comparison: 1519 defects ruled on, 1065 valid
THESE DISAGREE. The grader ruled on 1519 defects and the parsed
challenge lists hold 1523. On a tree written before
`parse_defects` stored the list, `challenge.json`'s `defects` is empty and
the grade's per-defect `type` is null with it — read the by-type split as
covering only the objections whose list WAS stored, and the (c) table's
counts, which come from the index, as the authority on how many there were.

A defect whose quotation failed the parse-time check is counted as alleged and
is never sent to the grader, so it can never be valid. `misattributed` is that
column; the probe measured flash inventing a defect on 15% of controls, and
this is where that shows up as a rate of this run's own.

